## Evidence

### Source Code Bug: Countdown Never Completes

The `updateCountdown` function has a critical path flaw in `/home/qg/workspace/apex-karts-64/game.js`:

```javascript
function updateCountdown(dt){
  if(GS.cdPhase===0)return;
  GS.cdTimer+=dt;
  if(GS.cdPhase===1){
    const phases=[{t:0.5,text:'3'},{t:1.5,text:'2'},{t:2.5,text:'1'},{t:3.5,text:'GO!'},{t:4.5,text:''}];
    for(let i=phases.length-1;i>=0;i--){
      if(GS.cdTimer>=phases[i].t){
        if(phases[i].text){showMsg(phases[i].text);if(phases[i].text==='GO!'){GS.cdPhase=2;GS.started=true;}}
        else{hideMsg();GS.cdPhase=3;}
        break;
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Once `cdPhase` transitions to **2** (on "GO!" at timer 3.5s), the `if(GS.cdPhase===1)` guard prevents any further advancement to phase 3. **Phase 2 has no handler**, so the countdown freezes permanently at "GO!".

### Physics Blocked by Phase Gate

```javascript
function updatePhysics(dt){
  if(!GS.started||GS.finished||GS.cdPhase<3)return;
  // ... kart movement, checkpoint tracking
}
```

Physics requires `cdPhase >= 3` to run. Since phase 3 is never reached, **physics never executes** — the kart never accelerates, never moves along the track, and checkpoints are never evaluated.

